 @cheshirster  Are you seriously trying to defend this product?! XD Like, you think you know better than literally every single expert review outlet?

You start by claiming that even with PCI-E 3.0, it is "faster than 1650 that is priced $500". If you had watched the review, you would see that the 1650 is within margin of error for average fps, and actually has a statistically significantly better 1% low performance (50 vs. 47 fps). Calling it faster than a 1650 (on PCI-E 3.0) is completely misleading here. Also, just because there are GTX 1650's for $500 doesn't make this card a good value. $500 for a GTX 1650 is absolutely outrageous, and I'm sure that not that many people would actually be willing to pay that much for one. The RX 6500 XT is going to be a bad value for most people, especially anybody who doesn't understand that it won't work properly without PCI-E 4.0.


The card could still be worth buying for some people who really need or really want a card now, if they can afford it, and if they understand what they're getting, (and it also depends upon what's available and what the prices actually are in their region) but that doesn't make this a good card. In general, it's a bad card. There will be MUCH better cards available for much more reasonable prices over the next year or two, at least in some regions.

